# Citation metadata for the precise software (Citation File Format 1.2.0, https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button generated from this file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use precise in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "precise: online covariance, correlation and precision matrix estimation in Python"
abstract: >-
  precise estimates covariance, correlation and precision matrices from a stream. Every estimator
  exposes an sklearn-style partial_fit, does a constant amount of work per observation, and keeps
  its state in a plain dictionary that can be checkpointed and restored. The package also scores
  estimates out of sample and recommends an estimator for a given data set. It depends on numpy
  alone.
authors:
  - family-names: Cotton
    given-names: Peter
    email: peter.cotton@microprediction.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1832-2924"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/microprediction/precise"
url: "https://precise.microprediction.org"
keywords:
  - covariance
  - correlation
  - precision matrix
  - online estimation
  - streaming
  - shrinkage
  - Ledoit-Wolf
